<title>HONG KONG: HK observatory reports quake east of Philippines.</title>
<headline>HK observatory reports quake east of Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake was detected east of the Philippines on Tuesday, the Royal Hong Kong Observatory said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The observatory said the quake, estimated at 5.6 on the Richter scale and recorded at 2034 local time (1234 GMT Tuesday), was located 310 km (190 miles) east-southeast of Cebu, the Philippines.</p>
